Every void call of a statement shares that statement's source range, and the
destructors a statement runs implicitly are void calls, so a removal of one was
emitted under the named call's identifier and reported against a line whose call
it never touched. The two are different mutations and are named apart: the
implicit destructor removals move to cxx_remove_implicit_destructor and
cxx_remove_void_call keeps the calls the source writes. Neither set loses a
mutant, the junk detector answers both kinds with the visitor that already
matches the statement's call expression, and cxx_calls carries both names so a
configuration naming that group is unchanged.
